2.2.evidence:
following— " (1) Application may be made to the Court for a protection order against a respondent in respect of alleged conduct, to—
(a) may be made by the spouse or parent who is the prescribed person in respect of whom the alleged conduct has been, or is likely to be, engaged in by the respondent;
(b) the respondent contravenes the order in any respect, the respondent commits an offence and is liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding ten thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both such fine and imprisonment.

